# Triality, the exceptional threefold symmetry of D four and Spin(8), modeled by the kernel. The double cover Spin(8) of the
# rotation group of eight-dimensional space has three inequivalent eight-dimensional irreducible representations: the vector
# 8v, the spinor 8s, and the cospinor 8c. They are the same size, eight, the one place in all dimensions where the vector and
# the two half-spinors match, two cubed against eight. TRIALITY is the outer automorphism group of Spin(8), the symmetric
# group on three letters, S3, that PERMUTES these three eight-dimensional pieces. It is unique to dimension eight and exists
# in no other rank. It is the threefold symmetry of the D four Coxeter-Dynkin diagram, the three outer nodes around one
# center, and it splits the twenty-four roots of the 24-cell into three classes of eight, 8v plus 8s plus 8c is twenty-four.
# This threefold rotation of the substrate's directions is the structure that gives the mesh its free spin.
#
# This file models the three representations and the two generators of their symmetry: a CYCLE of order three, the rotation
# vector to spinor to cospinor and back, and a SWAP of order two, the reflection exchanging spinor and cospinor while fixing
# the vector. It proves the cycle has order three, the swap is an involution, the vector is the fixed point of the swap, and
# the two generators satisfy the S3 relation that makes the group the symmetric group of order six, not the cyclic group.

load @term/seed/code/atom/flag
  find flag

# The three eight-dimensional irreducible representations of Spin(8): the vector 8v, the spinor 8s, and the cospinor 8c.
form rep
  case vector
  case spinor
  case cospinor

# TEMPLATE: one entry of a single-valued map out of a representation, `from` sent to the construction `to`. One definition
# serves both the cycle and the swap, so each reads as its permutation table.
tree map-rep
  take from
  take to

  hook fuse
    case {from}
      send back
        make {to}

# The order-three triality rotation: vector to spinor, spinor to cospinor, cospinor back to vector. This is the three-cycle
# generator of S3, the rotation of the three outer nodes of the D four diagram.
task cycle
  take r, like rep
  like rep
  fork case, read r
    fuse map-rep, vector, spinor
    fuse map-rep, spinor, cospinor
    fuse map-rep, cospinor, vector

# The order-two triality reflection: swap the spinor and the cospinor, fix the vector. This is the transposition generator of
# S3. The vector is its fixed point, the asymmetry that singles out the vector representation among the three.
task swap
  take r, like rep
  like rep
  fork case, read r
    fuse map-rep, vector, vector
    fuse map-rep, spinor, cospinor
    fuse map-rep, cospinor, spinor

# THE CYCLE HAS ORDER THREE: cycle (cycle (cycle r)) = r, for every representation. Applying the triality rotation three
# times returns each piece to itself. This is the threefold triality, the order-three relation of the three-cycle generator.
rule cycle-has-order-three
  mark r, like rep
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call cycle, read r
        link cycle
        link cycle
      read r
  fold r

# THE SWAP IS AN INVOLUTION: swap (swap r) = r, for every representation. Exchanging the spinor and the cospinor twice is the
# identity, the defining property of the reflection generator.
rule swap-is-an-involution
  mark r, like rep
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call swap, read r
        link swap
      read r
  fold r

# THE VECTOR IS THE FIXED POINT OF THE SWAP: swap vector = vector. The reflection fixes the vector and exchanges the two
# half-spinors. This asymmetry is what distinguishes the vector representation from the spinor and the cospinor.
rule vector-is-the-fixed-point-of-the-swap
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call swap
        make vector
      make vector
  calm hold

# THE SPINOR AND THE COSPINOR ARE EXCHANGED BY THE SWAP: swap spinor = cospinor. The two half-spinors are the moved points
# of the reflection, the pair triality treats as a mirror image.
rule spinor-and-cospinor-are-exchanged-by-the-swap
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call swap
        make spinor
      make cospinor
  calm hold

# THE S3 RELATION: swap (cycle (swap r)) = cycle (cycle r), for every representation. Conjugating the three-cycle by the
# transposition inverts it, and the inverse of the cycle is the cycle squared. This is the dihedral relation s c s = c
# inverse, which together with the order-three cycle and the involution swap presents the symmetric group S3 of order six.
# It shows the triality group is NOT the cyclic group of order three: the swap genuinely reverses the rotation.
rule triality-group-is-the-symmetric-group
  mark r, like rep
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call swap
        call cycle
          call swap
            read r
      call cycle, read r
        link cycle
  fold r

# THE CYCLE-SWAP PRODUCT HAS ORDER TWO: swap (cycle (swap (cycle r))) = r, for every representation. The product of the
# transposition and the three-cycle is itself a transposition, so it squares to the identity. This is a second reflection of
# S3, confirming the group has the three transpositions and two rotations of the symmetric group, six elements in all.
rule cycle-swap-product-has-order-two
  mark r, like rep
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call swap
        call cycle
          call swap
            call cycle
              read r
      read r
  fold r

# TIE TO D FOUR AND THE 24-CELL: triality splits the twenty-four roots of D four into three classes of eight, the vector,
# the spinor, and the cospinor, 8 plus 8 plus 8 is twenty-four. The three eights are the three pieces the cycle rotates.
hold triality-splits-the-twenty-four-roots-into-three-eights
  call is-equal
    code 24
    call add
      call add
        code 8
        code 8
      code 8

# THE THREE REPRESENTATIONS HAVE THE SAME SIZE EIGHT, TWO CUBED: 8 = 2*2*2. This common size, the vector matching the
# half-spinor, is the dimension-eight coincidence that lets triality permute the three on equal footing.
hold the-three-representations-have-size-eight
  call is-equal
    code 8
    call multiply
      call multiply
        code 2
        code 2
      code 2
